// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6168 add sigma rules for Windows Sandbox
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6168
// Pull request author: unrooted
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Fileless Execution Via Windows Sandbox CLI Inline LogonCommand
// Sigma ID: 3d9ac57f-46ea-4e59-a581-a59f61bb3a18
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Konrad 'unrooted' Klawikowski
// Date: 2026-07-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1564.006
// Description: Detects use of wsb.exe (Windows Sandbox CLI, available on Windows 11 24H2 and later) to launch a
//   sandbox from an inline XML configuration that contains an embedded <LogonCommand>.
// False positives:
//   - Developers or QA pipelines that spawn ad-hoc sandboxes from inline XML configurations for build verification
//   - Power users who script Sandbox usage to avoid maintaining .wsb files
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/security/application-security/application-isolation/windows-sandbox/windows-sandbox-cli
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Wsb/
//   - https://github.com/secdev02/SandBoxShenanigans
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e690cf7a8be81d20e2688ad8cc3866640f1d8fce/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wsb_inline_logoncommand.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\wsb.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wsb.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--config" and ProcessCommandLine contains "<LogonCommand>")
